<div xmlns:perseus="http://www.perseus.org/meta/perseus.rdfs#" xmlns:dctype="http://purl.org/dc/dcmitype/" xmlns:tufts="http://www.tufts.edu/" xmlns:alph="http://alpheios.net/namespaces/tei" class="alpheios-lex-text_container en">
    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n11874" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπέοικα</span></b> , <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>A.</b><i>to be unlike, differ from,</i> c. gen., <i><span class="en">
				Plu.
				<u>Per.</u>
				8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Arr.
				<u>Ind.</u>
				6.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Lib.
				<u>Or.</u>
				59.157
			</span></i>:—in early writers found only in part.
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπεοικώς</span></b> , 
				Att.
			
			<b><span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπεικώς</span></b> , <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">υῖα</span>, <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ός</span>,
				<i>unreasonable, unnatural,</i>
			<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἀπεικός</span> (
				v.l.
				<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπεοικός</span>
			) <i><span class="en">
				Hp.
				<u>VM</u>
				4
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				Antipho
				2.2.5
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἀπεικός</span> not
				<i>unlikely,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				2.62.8
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Philostr.
				<u>VA</u>
				3.34
			</span></i>; <span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπεοικὼς πρὸς τὰ καλά</span>
			<i>unfitted, indisposed</i> for noble deeds, <i><span class="en">
				Plb.
				6.26.12
			</span></i>: c. dat., <i>unlike,</i>
			<i><span class="en">
				Heph.
				15.4
			</span></i>. Adv.
			
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπεοικότως</span>”
				<i>unreasonably,</i>
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					6.55
				</span></i>
			; but 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">οὐκ ἀπεικότως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					Th.
					1.73
				</span></i>
			, <i><span class="en">
				2.8
			</span></i>, <i><span class="en">
				8.68
			</span></i>, cf. <i><span class="en">
				Porph.
				<u>Abst.</u>
				1.46
			</span></i>; <i><span class="en">
				D.Chr.
			</span></i> has 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπεοικότως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					12.35
				</span></i>
			, 
				“<span class="alpheios-lex-greek" lang="grc">ἀπεικότως</span>”
				 <i><span class="en">
					31.116
				</span></i>
			.</div>
